{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"docs.branch.test serves the supplied documentation tree on TCP port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct requests to the node on port 8080 returned HTTP 200 for both supplied documentation files and byte-matched the staged originals, including after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ab91827ae137458b","cmd-318d9610253244eb","cmd-4a2e59ef207d4a7c"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"orders.branch.test serves the supplied orders tree on the same TCP port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct requests on port 8080 returned HTTP 200 for both supplied orders files and byte-matched the staged originals, including after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ab91827ae137458b","cmd-318d9610253244eb","cmd-4a2e59ef207d4a7c"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"An unknown Host header receives an error instead of either tenant's content.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Unknown-host requests returned HTTP 404 and matched neither tenant index before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ab91827ae137458b","cmd-75d6d25788e349dd","cmd-318d9610253244eb","cmd-4a2e59ef207d4a7c"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve the approved content staged under /srv/legacy2/name-based-web-tenants.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All five staged-file hashes matched the authored baseline after configuration, and the complete aggregate hashset was unchanged across reboot. SELinux labels changed intentionally to permit serving, without changing file bytes.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-5ab559108aa14be8","cmd-f660d1091b45406b","cmd-318d9610253244eb","cmd-4a2e59ef207d4a7c"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained AlmaLinux 9.6 on kernel 5.14.0-570.12.1.el9_6 before and after execution. Apache and supporting utilities came from enabled AlmaLinux 9 repositories, and package consistency remained healthy.","evidence_ids":["cmd-15ff6d55d442493f","cmd-3938ac31f0594f44","cmd-4a2e59ef207d4a7c","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.94,"summary":"The task-related mutations—package installation, Apache configuration, SELinux labeling, service enablement, firewall opening for 8080, and the required restart—have clear causal roles. The failed apachectl -S invocation did not represent an abandoned experiment: the same command had already installed the final configuration and labels, and the configuration was subsequently validated. One unnecessary retained mutation remains: enabling stock Apache also left it listening on TCP port 80, although the task required only port 8080 and firewalld did not open port 80. This listener was introduced when Apache was enabled and remained after reboot. No failed services, damaged package state, or abandoned temporary files were observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3938ac31f0594f44","cmd-f53aa75d336749a5","cmd-bbd3ccb47fad4926","cmd-75d6d25788e349dd","cmd-63490bcc7d5e41bc","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for node1: a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, the restart was acknowledged, the post-restart boot identity differed and agreed with the fixed lifecycle snapshot, and Apache, port 8080, firewall state, tenant routing, error handling, content, SELinux enforcement, OS release, and kernel recovered correctly.","limitations":["The post-restart preservation check reports one aggregate hashset rather than repeating every individual hash, but it coherently matches the pre-restart aggregate and the individually verified baseline hashes.","Apache's unnecessary port-80 listener is a hygiene issue, not a demonstrated failure of the required port-8080 tenant behavior."]}
